{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1442385198,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDY0MzgzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140643833"},"message":"So, look for a git-annex branch instead?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442402192,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDcxMDgyOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140710829"},"message":"I guess... but it might still be among remote branches\n\nOn September 16, 2015 2:33:18 AM EDT, bpoldrack notifications@github.com wrote:\n\n\u003e So, look for a git-annex branch instead?\n\u003e \n\u003e ---\n\u003e \n\u003e Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub:\n\u003e https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140643833","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1442402977,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDcxMzAyNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140713026"},"message":"Right. Okay.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442407102,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDcyOTQ3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140729472"},"message":"note that annex itself doesn't run 'annex init' in non-annex repo -- it would just exit with\n\n```\n(git)hopa:~deb/bats[debian]git\n$\u003e git annex get .\ngit-annex: First run: git-annex init\n```\n\nbut if repository is annexed (there is a remote git-annex branch), then it does something (not necessarily full blown 'annex init', I just don't know and not sure if we could rely on that assumption) to make remote git-annex branch usable.  If no remote git-annex branch available among any remotes -- it asks to run init","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1442413178,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc1NTI1Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140755252"},"message":"Re 'read-only' from #205 \nI'm absolutely fine with the different detection of whether a repo is an annex as described above.\nWhat I don't really get is: What else besides the information \"this is an annex\" do you imagine to read from an annex without calling an annex-init?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442413613,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc1NzUyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140757528"},"message":"ideally I just need a command which would tell me that a file is under annex control (thus doesn't work for direct mode atm since I rely on git to tell me that), then discover what is the root dir of that Annex, then to check if it has content (we have one already), and then request content (we have that one already too)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442413799,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc1ODk1OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140758958"},"message":"actually let's just ask @joeyh :  is there an annex command I could run on an arbitrary file in an arbitrary directory to figure out if it is under control of annex (rooted somewhere above, and possibly in the direct mode, thus not just a symlink to .git/annex/objects)? and then (or at the same time) to figure out the root directory (we could traverse up until hitting .git but I bet annex does it already as well and better, respecting $GIT_DIR etc) of that annex repo?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1442414977,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc2NDU1MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140764551"},"message":"Well, my point is the question whether annex would be able to tell about an annexed file without invoking 'init'. That's what I try to understand regarding \"read-only\".\n\nAs for the functionality itself: What about checking get_file_key()? No key, no annex, right?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442415343,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc2NjYxMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140766611"},"message":"On Wed, 16 Sep 2015, bpoldrack wrote:\n\n\u003e Well, my point is the question whether annex would be able to tell about an\n\u003e annexed file without invoking 'init'. That's what I try to understand regarding\n\u003e \"read-only\".\n\u003e \n\u003e As for the functionality itself: What about checking get_file_key()? No key, no\n\u003e annex, right?\n\nthat should work indeed!  so we just need to figure out for a file what\nis the possible repo root  dir.... we could check if a symlink (would\nwork only on non-crippled FS) and points to somewhere in .git/annex and\nbroken then it must be in annex and indirect mode, and we can\nfigure out topdir and get it.  If file is not a symlink and for direct\nmode/crippled FS I guess we need to traverse up to find .git and then\nuse get_file_key()","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1442417756,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc3OTczNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140779735"},"message":"To me it's just not clear where to do the detection of the root dir. \ndatalad commands should work like git/git-annex commands. So, most of them should figure out where they are in anyway and get a fitting repo instance (see cmdline/helpers/get_repo_instance). I'm not sure at what point we would need to use the automagic without already knowing the root dir.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442419703,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc4OTk0MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140789940"},"message":"ah -- cool. missed that `get_repo_instance`. could/should use it I guess. minor wishlist comment then what if it would accept path to be a path to file -- would it may be beneficial may be inspect if a symlink and where it points to and if to '(../)+/.git/' take that path?  or you don't expect any speedups from that logic?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1442420298,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc5MjI2MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140792261"},"message":"git annex info run on a file will tell you that. It didn't work in\ndirect mode until recently; does now.\n\nAs to finding the top of the git repository: git rev-parse --git-dir\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442420323,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc5MjM0NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140792345"},"message":"@joeyh cool, thanks!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442420387,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MDc5MjYyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/204#issuecomment-140792620"},"message":"@bpoldrack meanwhile RFed to use `get_repo_instance` in bbf6a7793cfe0c06df071215026530ad85dfa8fd BUT then we get back to needing to detect not-yet-inited annexrepo as annexrepo (test would fail now ) ;)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"t